{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1064743-signs-of-sorcery-release-date","id":1064743,"title":"Signs of Sorcery Release date?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-19T07:30:09-07:00","id":1064743,"title":"Signs of Sorcery Release date?","content":"Does anyone know when its coming out as a PDF? Any clue as to how much it will cost? Really excited about this book!<br /> <br /> Also, I recently started a recruitment thread for a Mage PbP over on GITP if anyones interested. We need a ST! links here: <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?518772-Game-Request-Mage-The-Awakening-2nd-Edition&amp;p=21825129#post21825129\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showt...9#post21825129</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T08:22:31-07:00","id":1064761,"title":"","content":"&quot;When it's done&quot; and &quot;About 20 dollars US for a PDF&quot; are the usual answers. Hard deadlines aren't something the nature of the industry allows for, and Dave's got Signs, Tome of the Pentacle, Deviant, and a Beast book in his inbox, last I heard, so patience is probably called for. Even if it went to Mike tomorrow, it'll be a month or three at least before it gets through art and layout, depending on the backlog.<br /> <br /> Patience is the order of the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T08:27:25-07:00","id":1064762,"title":"","content":"Ahh, I saw it was under the Jan/Feb/March section of the release schedule and got all excited.I will embrace patience as much as I possibly can. <br /> Looking forward to more of the Wizard of Aus actual play by the way, sounds like a great game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T08:42:00-07:00","id":1064769,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I am actually in the middle of writing up the next few posts for it right now. The game actually just finished the first arc yesterday and began its second, so I'm playing catch-up on it all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T08:42:11-07:00","id":1064770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1064743-signs-of-sorcery-release-date?p=1064762#post1064762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh, I saw it was under the Jan/Feb/March section of the release schedule and got all excited.I will embrace patience as much as I possibly can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the estimated windows in on the Current Works page are never anywhere near accurate. I'm surprised they still put those up at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T14:40:32-07:00","id":1064930,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of surprised that they're working on the book AFTER SoS. That seems strange. But I'll admit I didn't know that he was also working on Beast and Deviant. That's quite a bit to put on one person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T15:02:24-07:00","id":1064939,"title":"","content":"The problem isn't patience or Onyx's inability to give a date, the problem is that after the whole Paradox buyout we are all feeling a little gun shy.<br /> \u200bThey've done their best to reassure us but the fear, either of really long delays or the game lines being ripped out from under them, won't subside until we see everything is moving smoothly again on these games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T15:07:07-07:00","id":1064943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1064743-signs-of-sorcery-release-date?p=1064939#post1064939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem isn't patience or Onyx's inability to give a date, the problem is that after the whole Paradox buyout we are all feeling a little gun shy.<br /> \u200bThey've done their best to reassure us but the fear, either of really long delays or the game lines being ripped out from under them, won't subside until we see everything is moving smoothly again on these games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really long delays wouldn't be a new thing under Paradox's management, but I do see what you mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T15:47:04-07:00","id":1064969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1064743-signs-of-sorcery-release-date?p=1064939#post1064939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem isn't patience or Onyx's inability to give a date, the problem is that after the whole Paradox buyout we are all feeling a little gun shy.<br /> \u200bThey've done their best to reassure us but the fear, either of really long delays or the game lines being ripped out from under them, won't subside until we see everything is moving smoothly again on these games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox doesn't really seem to be dragging out approvals and, even if that were the issue, their approvals come later in the process.<br /> <br /> Plus, OPP has contracts for a lease for a given term. Unless they really fuck up somehow, Paradox isn't just going to rip the license away.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T16:05:19-07:00","id":1064982,"title":"","content":"I stopped asking about Signs of Sorcery. Pestering Dave or anyone else at OPP will not get the book released any quicker or provide us with a firm release date, and all it accomplishes is annoying Dave.<br /> <br /> I'm simply hopeful it will be released before the end of the year, and if we're very, very lucky, by GenCon. I am optimistic, but remain realistic about OPP release dates.<br /> <br /> I would also love to see Tome of the Pentacle added to the Monday Meeting Notes. As a native New Yorker, I'm anxious to see the full setting write-up for NYC.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T06:22:51-07:00","id":1065212,"title":"","content":"Hmm, so the Mage developer has been burdened with Deviant development as well. I gave very little attention to the latter line so far, therefore I was not mindful of that. Well, this in combination with SoS getting stalled while they finished the 2e rulebook might help explain why SoS has languished in development for a year, which by apparent OPP standards about many other CoD, WoD, Trinity, and Scion books seemed a remarkable delay to me (I have negative interest in Exalted so I paid no attention to Ex3 drama).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T09:26:56-07:00","id":1065284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1064743-signs-of-sorcery-release-date?p=1065212#post1065212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, so the Mage developer has been burdened with Deviant development as well..</div> </div> </div> </div>Although time consuming and low paying, I don't believe Dave views his role as the developer of Deviant or Mage as a &quot;burden.&quot; In fact, precisely because of the low pay and resource demands, they're likely labors of love.<br /> <br /> While I, too, am anxious for the release of Signs of Sorcery, it's not stalled, nor is it late in comparison to other CofD supplements. For instance, Secrets of the Covenants, the first Requiem supplement was only just released, and Requiem was published <i>years</i> before Awakening 2e.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T09:27:40-07:00","id":1065285,"title":"","content":"&quot;Burdened&quot; seems like a curious word choice. I imagine Dave took the project because he was interested in it, not because it was assigned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T09:51:12-07:00","id":1065289,"title":"","content":"If he is not payed for it he doesn't need to do it. It's obvious. The problem is that FAQ and <i>multiple</i> erratas are part of publishing a game. Look at any of the popular rpgs or board games. They all have it and I doubt that everywhere it is an unpaid work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T10:34:04-07:00","id":1065304,"title":"","content":"Deviant's not a burden. It's a priviledge. What I'm not paid for is being here and responding to threads like this. That's something I'm perfectly happy to do given time, but understand that my priorities are elsewhere right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T10:43:47-07:00","id":1065312,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> And I'm thankful for your response. Can you give us some rough estimation of FAQ arrival and if its gonna be a one time thing or something updatable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T10:45:47-07:00","id":1065315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1064743-signs-of-sorcery-release-date?p=1065304#post1065304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviant's not a burden. It's a priviledge. What I'm not paid for is being here and responding to threads like this. That's something I'm perfectly happy to do given time, but understand that my priorities are elsewhere right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that feeling,Wishing you the best of luck","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T11:03:51-07:00","id":1065317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1064743-signs-of-sorcery-release-date?p=1065312#post1065312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> And I'm thankful for your response. Can you give us some rough estimation of FAQ arrival and if its gonna be a one time thing or something updatable?</div> </div> </div> </div>At this juncture, I wouldn't be surprised if the FAQ was released after Signs of Sorcery, as I expect the latter to answer at least some of our questions.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> : When might Tome of the Pentacle begin first drafts, and is there anything firm planned for after TotP? Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T11:19:34-07:00","id":1065326,"title":"","content":"TotP will go into first drafts once Signs is in editing. Mage has one more approved book after that, but it's not been announced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T11:26:00-07:00","id":1065330,"title":"","content":"Heh.<br /> (characters)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T11:44:01-07:00","id":1065335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1064743-signs-of-sorcery-release-date?p=1065284#post1065284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although time consuming and low paying, I don't believe Dave views his role as the developer of Deviant or Mage as a &quot;burden.&quot; In fact, precisely because of the low pay and resource demands, they're likely labors of love.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most certainly, and rest assured I did not wish to imply otherwise, nor disrespect anyone and anything about the persons, items, works, and gamelines involved. It's just that even the labors of love one can task oneself with can become more or less ... onerous? time- and resource-consuming? hard ? for a person, no matter how willingly and passionately they may engage so. I meant 'burdensome' in a neutral, not negative sense. Geez, folks, it's the same turn of words I'd use if I see a writer or artist self-imposing oneself a big amount of creative work, or a volunteer doing the same about charity work. If anyone found anything offensive or improper about my choice of words, accept my apologies, blame cultural and linguistic differences, and let's move on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While I, too, am anxious for the release of Signs of Sorcery, it's not stalled, nor is it late in comparison to other CofD supplements. For instance, Secrets of the Covenants, the first Requiem supplement was only just released, and Requiem was published <i>years</i> before Awakening 2e. </div> </div> </div>True, but I do not even dare making any schedule assumptions at all about products that did not yet reach first draft stage. I just try to eyeball them about stuff that is at some point of the release schedule, from first draft to proofing. According to my own perception and monitoring of the Monday Meeting Notes, SoS seemed to be significantly slower than several other products that had entered the pipeline at similar times, and I wondered about the reason. Up to 2e finalization, I thought they had mostly suspended working on it, since it promises to be a rather crunchy-heavy book, until they had the basic rules set in stone as a necessary groundwork. And I wondered what was the issue after that, if say parts of SoS had required rewriting at the development stage or somesuch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-20-2017, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T12:11:00-07:00","id":1065352,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1949\" data-vbnamecard=\"1949\">Irioth</a> : It's become readily apparent over the last few years that it's almost to be expected that some projects will apparently languish at certain points, usually final development, art direction or approval. OPP does not provide explanations and they've made clear there are no promised release dates.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I imagine that items such as Kickstarter reward and bonus content, materials that have been paid for, have priority on the schedule. OPP is a tiny company, often further restrained by license requirements, and even a small shift in resources or personnel can mean a project's release might be pushed back months or more.<br /> <br /> Take some solace that Signs of Sorcery is hardly unique. Many of us are also anxiously awaiting books like Changeling 2e, the Dark Eras Companion, A Thousand Years of Night and others that have been &quot;delayed&quot; longer than SoS.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T12:52:45-07:00","id":1065375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1064743-signs-of-sorcery-release-date?p=1065352#post1065352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1949\" data-vbnamecard=\"1949\">Irioth</a> : It's become readily apparent over the last few years that it's almost to be expected that some projects will apparently languish at certain points, usually final development, art direction or approval. OPP does not provide explanations and they've made clear there are no promised release dates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know. There is scarcely a more avid reader of the MMN than me, and often some info about why a project is apparently delayed is provided there, even if it's just 'artist shenanigans' or Paradox folks taking their time for approval. This often helps tone down my impatience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Additionally, I imagine that items such as Kickstarter reward and bonus content, materials that have been paid for, have priority on the schedule. OPP is a tiny company, often further restrained by license requirements, and even a small shift in resources or personnel can mean a project's release might be pushed back months or more. </div> </div> </div>True as well, admittedly the Kickstarter stuff may have gotten me a little spoiled, since a lot of OPP material gets produced that way nowadays, I have been a patron for most OPP Kickstarters, and you often get more info on their production state through KS updates than other books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take some solace that Signs of Sorcery is hardly unique. Many of us are also anxiously awaiting books like Changeling 2e, the Dark Eras Companion, A Thousand Years of Night and others that have been &quot;delayed&quot; longer than SoS. </div> </div> </div>Well, true about the general point, but about relative lengths of delay I find your comment funny since my perception has been the opposite. As a matter of fact, I have been using the fact books like Book of Secrets, Dark Ages Companion, C20, and A Thousand Years of Night are apparently closer to release (crosses fingers) as consolation for my frustration about SoS. These are among the other books I'm greatly interested in, so I've been closely monitoring MMN for them all. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T13:16:15-07:00","id":1065384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1064743-signs-of-sorcery-release-date?p=1065375#post1065375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, true about the general point, but about relative lengths of delay I find your comment funny since my perception has been the opposite. As a matter of fact, I have been using the fact books like Book of Secrets, Dark Ages Companion, C20, and A Thousand Years of Night are apparently closer to release (crosses fingers) as consolation for my frustration about SoS. These are among the other books I'm greatly interested in, so I've been closely monitoring MMN for them all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>All the mentioned books sans ATYON are related to Kickstarter WOD projects, and thus will have resource and scheduling priority. Don't compare them to non-Kickstarter CofD projects (and don't get spoiled<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). <br /> <br /> As to ATYON, keep in mind that the project has been around for<i> years</i>, and is only very recently proceeding apace because OPP brought in a new Requiem developer (or co-developer with Rose?). In the world of OPP CofD supplements, Signs of Sorcery is &quot;on schedule,&quot; at least to the extent that term has any real meaning.<br /> <br /> We simply need to be patient. I expect we'll shortly find ourselves pleasantly surprised when SoS leaves &quot;development,&quot; and then dismayed once again as it sits in the purgatory of &quot;art direction&quot; and WW/Paradox approval. The book will come when it's &quot;ready,&quot; and not a moment before. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T03:57:22-07:00","id":1065660,"title":"","content":"I want to remind you we had <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sariras-relics-of-ascension-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">S&amp;S spoiler on Sariras</a> 'only' dozen weeks ago. For the nowdays speed of work in OPP, it's 'lighting fast'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T05:18:21-07:00","id":1065690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1064743-signs-of-sorcery-release-date?p=1065660#post1065660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to remind you we had <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/sariras-relics-of-ascension-mage-the-awakening/&quot;]S&amp;S</a> spoiler on Sariras[/URL] 'only' dozen weeks ago. For the nowdays speed of work in OPP, it's 'lighting fast'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Holy crap, how did I miss this? Awesome stuff! And some Obrimos related magic that doesn't seem to hate Obrimos! 2nd Ed is waaaaaay better at that so far, I remember that in 1e it always felt like some of the books had a real hate-on for the Obrimos <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T18:14:36-07:00","id":1066077,"title":"","content":"Some of the books make it as they fall on the schedule. Some come out the next season. There have been specific reasons that caused certain books to get behind and lags in lines. Brookshaw seems smart enough to have drafting stages of books overlap with the stages that require more of his attention with other books. No reason to believe one book could delay another by more than a week. Have a little faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}